# 52 (regime 3): a disjunction-guarded recursive schema gets past the
# cycle detector, works for the base case, and dies on the FIRST level
# of real nesting -- with an error naming neither the recursion nor
# the schema.
#
# run: node ../../../ts/bin/aontu.js guarded-next-breaks-at-depth-one.aon
# run: aontu-go guarded-next-breaks-at-depth-one.aon
#
# expected: {"t":{"next":{"next":null,"v":2},"v":1}}
# actual (both ports):
#   [aontu/scalar_kind]: Cannot unify values at path $.t.next
#
# The recursive alternative ($.Node) does not re-resolve at the nested
# position, so the disjunct is left holding only `null` against the
# nested map. With `next: null` instead of a nested node, the document
# evaluates -- the base case is fine, which is what makes the failure
# look like the data's fault rather than the schema's.
Node: hide({v: integer, next: null | $.Node})
t: $.Node & {v: 1, next: {v: 2, next: null}}
